^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
found no match for symbol 'take'
invalid implicit conversion from 'char \[6l\]' to 'struct basic_string'
--
Regression for `char[N]` -> `const std::string&` implicit
conversion in argument position, when `<sstream>` (or any header
that fully elaborates `std::basic_string`) is in the translation
unit.  Sister test to cpp11_string_default_arg_sstream.

Without the fallback, CBMC reports
  found no match for symbol 'take'
because no viable converting constructor for `char[N]` ->
`std::string` exists in the components list.  Fixed by
extending the existing implicit_typecast workaround to
user_defined_conversion_sequence so reference bindings benefit
from the same fallback.
